WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:02.045
Lolly Tools

00:00:03.041 --> 00:00:07.143
Powerfully reproducible assets & tools.

00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:11.193
Deterministic, fast, open-source platform

00:00:11.225 --> 00:00:13.269
- bring your own brand.

00:00:14.035 --> 00:00:15.818
Try it now.

00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:19.067
lolly-tools runs in the browser and

00:00:19.121 --> 00:00:21.618
installs as an app.

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:25.193
Nothing you make ever leaves your device

00:00:25.251 --> 00:00:27.043
without your say.

00:00:27.815 --> 00:00:30.690
Desktop, mobile and command-line builds

00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:33.244
are on the releases page.

00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:35.793
Read first.

00:00:36.561 --> 00:00:38.478
The platform is explained at

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:42.207
lolly-tools/info, with one door each for

00:00:42.268 --> 00:00:45.349
creators, builders and operators, a

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:48.461
quickstart, and the trust pages that back

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:50.695
each claim with the mechanism that

00:00:50.754 --> 00:00:52.419
enforces it.

00:00:53.212 --> 00:00:56.343
We built Lolly for ourselves.

00:00:57.146 --> 00:01:00.491
SUSE needed thousands of on-brand files,

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:03.745
each with its name sealed inside, made

00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:06.124
without handing anything to outside

00:01:06.188 --> 00:01:07.569
services.

00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:11.303
So we built a tool that does all of it on

00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:14.615
the device, and released it as open

00:01:14.719 --> 00:01:17.520
source, like everything else we make.

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:21.487
We keep maintaining it because we use it

00:01:21.552 --> 00:01:22.894
every day.

00:01:23.669 --> 00:01:26.533
There is no obligation: everything here

00:01:26.597 --> 00:01:29.119
works with or without us.

00:01:30.266 --> 00:01:32.565
What is Lolly Tools

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.715
A platform that hosts a library of small,

00:01:36.804 --> 00:01:39.946
focused tools that produce deterministic

00:01:40.006 --> 00:01:41.820
creative assets.

00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:45.619
Users need no design skill, no vendor

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:49.005
lock-in and no internet to render, and the

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.877
platform is designed to add premium

00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:54.836
production-quality rendering certainty to

00:01:54.908 --> 00:01:56.695
variable data.

00:01:57.447 --> 00:02:00.888
It's also your personal DAM - every logo,

00:02:00.966 --> 00:02:03.657
palette, font and upload lives in an

00:02:03.735 --> 00:02:06.528
on-device catalog, hydrated and

00:02:06.632 --> 00:02:09.220
supercharged by your design system and

00:02:09.284 --> 00:02:10.469
tools.

00:02:11.249 --> 00:02:14.393
Tools can be used via a:

00:02:15.185 --> 00:02:18.204
Web app - installable offline progressive

00:02:18.268 --> 00:02:19.197
web app

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:24.493
Mobile and Desktop installable packages.

00:02:25.261 --> 00:02:27.991
and of course, the Command Line - plus a

00:02:28.082 --> 00:02:30.969
full-screen terminal UI «TUI».

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.468
Organisation services are optional.

00:02:36.271 --> 00:02:38.836
lolly-work is part of the same Lolly

00:02:38.899 --> 00:02:41.505
project, maintained and deployed

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:42.844
separately.

00:02:43.598 --> 00:02:47.033
Pair it with these apps for OIDC SSO, SCIM

00:02:47.094 --> 00:02:49.335
provisioning, group permissions, shared

00:02:49.395 --> 00:02:52.169
catalogs and projects, work collabs,

00:02:52.218 --> 00:02:54.381
approvals, governed delivery, server

00:02:54.441 --> 00:02:57.120
render jobs and audit records.

00:02:57.919 --> 00:03:01.743
Standalone Lolly remains independent.

00:03:02.552 --> 00:03:05.742
See organisation use and deployment for

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.756
the split, including which data reaches

00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:10.269
the service.

00:03:11.405 --> 00:03:15.318
Why deploy Lolly in your organization?

00:03:16.104 --> 00:03:18.779
Hard-coded constraints of design

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.293
decisions.

00:03:21.081 --> 00:03:23.789
Free, open-source platform - the engine,

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:26.596
every shell, the schemas and docs are

00:03:26.662 --> 00:03:29.244
MPL-2 point 0.

00:03:30.021 --> 00:03:33.567
Tools and assets are just data: bring your

00:03:33.631 --> 00:03:36.638
own brand content «SUSE's tool & asset

00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:39.566
packs are proprietary - see Licensing &

00:03:39.627 --> 00:03:40.894
structure».

00:03:41.668 --> 00:03:44.970
Unlimited scale, No SaaS fees.

00:03:45.771 --> 00:03:49.603
Low-or-Zero server costs: Lolly uses local

00:03:49.665 --> 00:03:51.419
device compute.

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:55.416
Builds for Mac, Windows, Linux, iOS,

00:03:55.476 --> 00:03:58.120
Android, web and the command line.

00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:02.936
Huge format support - 50 in, 56 out «35

00:04:02.995 --> 00:04:05.542
round-trip; the live register is

00:04:05.613 --> 00:04:09.479
docs/site/formats-catalog-json, and

00:04:09.558 --> 00:04:12.895
tests/readme-formats-test-ts keeps these

00:04:12.976 --> 00:04:15.345
three numbers pinned to it».

00:04:16.091 --> 00:04:19.648
Export: SVG · EPS · CMYK EPS · EMF · DXF ·

00:04:19.706 --> 00:04:23.657
PDF · Print PDF «CMYK» · PPTX · PNG ·

00:04:23.711 --> 00:04:27.209
Animated PNG · JPEG · WebP · Animated WebP

00:04:27.242 --> 00:04:29.990
· AVIF · TIFF · CMYK TIFF · ICO · PSD ·

00:04:30.042 --> 00:04:33.248
EXR · Radiance HDR · MP4 · WebM · GIF ·

00:04:33.308 --> 00:04:37.379
Animated SVG · dotLottie · MP3 · M4A · WAV

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.329
· Opus · HTML · MD · TXT · CSV · JSON ·

00:04:41.392 --> 00:04:43.620
ICS · VCF · ZIP.

00:04:44.386 --> 00:04:48.721
Import adds layered PSD · PSB · XCF, HEIC,

00:04:48.793 --> 00:04:52.796
MOV, GLB · glTF, audio & tracker «OGG ·

00:04:52.876 --> 00:04:55.496
FLAC · MIDI · MOD» and live designs from

00:04:55.553 --> 00:04:58.845
Illustrator · InDesign · Figma · Penpot.

00:04:59.611 --> 00:05:03.032
EXR and Radiance HDR are floating-point

00:05:03.123 --> 00:05:06.629
HDR masters written through host-codec by

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.074
tools that compute float pixels, and via

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.941
the CLI - the web export picker does not

00:05:12.999 --> 00:05:14.370
offer them.

00:05:15.145 --> 00:05:17.639
AVIF encodes through the browser's own

00:05:17.709 --> 00:05:21.386
canvas-toBlob, and M4A · Opus through

00:05:21.447 --> 00:05:24.585
WebCodecs, so both depend on the browser

00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:25.694
build.

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:29.294
Plus design tokens & palettes - import

00:05:29.359 --> 00:05:34.164
DTCG and Tokens Studio; export DTCG ·

00:05:34.241 --> 00:05:37.619
ASE · GPL · CSS variables.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:41.942
Print-ready output: CMYK PDF & TIFF,

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:45.169
physical units, bleed, crop/registration

00:05:45.225 --> 00:05:48.310
marks, colour bars and press «FOGRA/SWOP»

00:05:48.371 --> 00:05:49.819
profiles.

00:05:50.587 --> 00:05:54.494
Infinite deterministic media creation.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.932
Renders and exports offline - the engine

00:05:57.988 --> 00:06:01.015
makes no network call, and the shells need

00:06:01.088 --> 00:06:04.257
none at render time once a tool's assets,

00:06:04.345 --> 00:06:07.164
fonts, shaping WASM and any on-device

00:06:07.223 --> 00:06:10.001
model have been fetched once «the PWA

00:06:10.083 --> 00:06:13.502
caches them on first use; Settings →

00:06:13.561 --> 00:06:16.720
Available offline pre-fetches the lot».

00:06:17.479 --> 00:06:21.228
«Optional MCP, CA, network integrations

00:06:21.323 --> 00:06:24.361
and lolly-work organisation services have

00:06:24.453 --> 00:06:26.604
separate data flows; see

00:06:26.671 --> 00:06:29.370
docs/server-surface-md.»

00:06:30.164 --> 00:06:32.993
Full command-line support.

00:06:33.772 --> 00:06:36.857
Save tokens, tell your model to try Lolly

00:06:36.951 --> 00:06:38.045
first!

00:06:39.178 --> 00:06:41.109
What this is not

00:06:42.076 --> 00:06:45.294
An unconstrained design suite.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.972
Lolly ships a real open canvas - the

00:06:49.034 --> 00:06:50.669
Design tool,

00:06:51.427 --> 00:06:55.014
with a pen, node editing, keyframes, decks

00:06:55.076 --> 00:06:57.592
and presenting - so "not a design tool"

00:06:57.623 --> 00:06:59.219
would be untrue.

00:06:59.999 --> 00:07:02.896
What it is not is a place to escape the

00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:06.373
brand: every colour, face and asset on

00:07:06.421 --> 00:07:09.580
that canvas is the brand's own, so free

00:07:09.641 --> 00:07:11.975
arrangement never becomes off-brand

00:07:12.047 --> 00:07:13.244
output.

00:07:14.018 --> 00:07:16.422
Ideation that has to leave the brand

00:07:16.483 --> 00:07:19.981
system belongs in Illustrator or Figma;

00:07:20.043 --> 00:07:22.162
the finished file comes back through

00:07:22.222 --> 00:07:25.358
Design's Import a design and becomes

00:07:25.447 --> 00:07:28.319
governed, reproducible output.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:32.312
See docs/positioning-md for the full

00:07:32.374 --> 00:07:34.269
market comparison.

00:07:35.402 --> 00:07:37.618
Repository layout

00:07:38.612 --> 00:07:41.427
lolly contains the engine, shells,

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:45.005
community tool pack, docs and the MCP and

00:07:45.073 --> 00:07:48.294
CA services as plain directories.

00:07:49.065 --> 00:07:52.644
The optional organisation service lives in

00:07:52.692 --> 00:07:55.669
the sibling lolly-work repository.

00:07:56.436 --> 00:07:59.749
The one exception is brands/suse, a

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.552
private git submodule: SUSE's tool and

00:08:02.623 --> 00:08:05.190
asset pack, which stays out of the public

00:08:05.253 --> 00:08:06.270
tree.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.893
Code example omitted.

00:08:10.655 --> 00:08:14.294
Critical separation: engine/ knows nothing

00:08:14.334 --> 00:08:15.944
about SUSE.

00:08:16.709 --> 00:08:19.094
Brand-specific content lives in brand

00:08:19.156 --> 00:08:21.953
packs «brands/suse - private;

00:08:22.016 --> 00:08:24.701
brands/lolly-start - the blank starter

00:08:24.762 --> 00:08:27.124
brand», brand-agnostic tools in

00:08:27.185 --> 00:08:31.088
community/; the shells, services, engine

00:08:31.149 --> 00:08:34.694
and docs are MPL-2 point 0.

00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:39.020
There is no repo-root tools//catalog/ view

00:08:39.077 --> 00:08:40.111
on disk:

00:08:40.173 --> 00:08:44.140
packages/node-shell/src/content-roots-ts

00:08:44.203 --> 00:08:46.565
resolves which tool pack and catalog a

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:50.019
build uses, from profiles-json, at runtime

00:08:50.051 --> 00:08:52.059
- contentRoots«», toolFile«»,

00:08:52.119 --> 00:08:54.985
catalogFile«», and materializeInto«» for

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:57.721
the one place a real copy is still needed

00:08:57.781 --> 00:09:00.895
«dist/, for static hosting».

00:09:01.683 --> 00:09:04.176
Set LOLLY_PROFILE=suse or

00:09:04.237 --> 00:09:07.144
LOLLY_PROFILE=lolly-start to choose

00:09:07.208 --> 00:09:10.690
explicitly; otherwise it resolves the same

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.160
way the old profile switcher did «the

00:09:13.221 --> 00:09:16.449
declared default, else the first profile

00:09:16.509 --> 00:09:18.944
whose packs are complete - lolly-start on

00:09:18.976 --> 00:09:22.506
a public clone, since brands/suse is

00:09:22.598 --> 00:09:23.794
absent».

00:09:24.931 --> 00:09:27.253
Architectural commitments

00:09:28.183 --> 00:09:31.169
These decisions are settled.

00:09:31.926 --> 00:09:34.661
Changing any of them is a major

00:09:34.744 --> 00:09:36.245
undertaking:

00:09:37.031 --> 00:09:39.368
Declarative tools.

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:44.669
A tool is a manifest + template + assets.

00:09:45.428 --> 00:09:48.481
Inputs are declared in the manifest, not

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.369
inferred from template tokens.

00:09:52.126 --> 00:09:55.506
hooks-js is an optional escape hatch for

00:09:55.585 --> 00:09:57.869
tools that need imperative behavior

00:09:57.939 --> 00:10:01.495
«chart-js rendering, QR encoding».

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:05.423
Tools and assets are data, not bundled

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:06.643
code.

00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:10.450
Clients sync them from a signed manifest

00:10:10.528 --> 00:10:11.918
URL.

00:10:12.722 --> 00:10:15.824
New tools and assets don't require app

00:10:15.865 --> 00:10:17.118
updates.

00:10:17.886 --> 00:10:20.243
Capability bridge.

00:10:21.022 --> 00:10:24.377
Tools never touch the filesystem, network

00:10:24.425 --> 00:10:27.668
or DOM-outside-template directly.

00:10:28.444 --> 00:10:31.368
They call a versioned host.

00:10:32.145 --> 00:10:34.694
* API.

00:10:35.446 --> 00:10:38.083
This is what makes the same tool work in

00:10:38.142 --> 00:10:40.695
browser, Tauri and CLI.

00:10:41.487 --> 00:10:44.768
Stable asset ID'S forever.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:50.119
suse/logo/primary is a contract.

00:10:50.921 --> 00:10:53.869
Never reuse, never rename.

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:57.371
Version in the manifest, never in the

00:10:57.442 --> 00:10:58.493
path.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.493
URL mode is first-class.

00:11:03.265 --> 00:11:06.587
Every input must be expressible as URL

00:11:06.649 --> 00:11:07.869
params.

00:11:08.632 --> 00:11:13.221
CLI mode = headless DOM «jsdom» + URL mode

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.219
+ file output.

00:11:16.012 --> 00:11:18.193
One render path.

00:11:18.996 --> 00:11:21.692
Storage via the bridge.

00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:24.906
Tools call host-state-save«» /

00:11:24.967 --> 00:11:26.744
host-state-load«».

00:11:27.506 --> 00:11:30.186
The bridge picks IndexedDB «web»,

00:11:30.258 --> 00:11:33.220
filesystem «Tauri» or memory «CLI».

00:11:33.984 --> 00:11:36.594
Tools never know which.

00:11:37.379 --> 00:11:39.768
Maturity tags.

00:11:40.546 --> 00:11:43.427
Every tool declares status: official |

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:46.069
community | experimental.

00:11:46.845 --> 00:11:49.414
Experimental tools watermark their

00:11:49.477 --> 00:11:50.794
exports.

00:11:51.564 --> 00:11:54.605
This is the structural answer to the risk

00:11:54.698 --> 00:11:57.419
that every tool in the gallery reads as

00:11:57.497 --> 00:11:59.644
carrying the same weight.

00:12:00.775 --> 00:12:02.571
